# Universe content · space tech: megastructures, stations, ships, drives, colonies
# researched: Wikipedia "Megastructure", "Dyson sphere"; NASA and Planetary Society propulsion
#   overviews (ion, solar sail, nuclear thermal); Aerospace Corp "Emerging In-Space Propulsion";
#   IEEE Spectrum on warp-drive physics; Kardashev scale (Kardashev 1964)
# The 100 kinds of colony and the 100-step travel ladder are on the public space page.
# Every built thing is generated live in the builder species' own image (LAW 14).
# Spec: docs/CONTENT-FORMAT.md · wiki/systems/r10-space.md · wiki/systems/r04b-generators.md

# ── How big a civilization's power is (Kardashev scale) ──

@scale type-1
name: Planetary civilization (Type I)
real: yes
says: uses all the energy reaching its home planet

@scale type-2
name: Stellar civilization (Type II)
real: yes
says: uses all the energy of its star, with a Dyson swarm or sphere

@scale type-3
name: Galactic civilization (Type III)
real: yes
says: uses the energy of its whole galaxy

# ── Megastructures ──

@mega dyson-swarm
name: Dyson swarm
real: hypothetical
says: a huge cloud of separate collectors and habitats orbiting a star, catching its light; the kind real scientists think is buildable

@mega dyson-bubble
name: Dyson bubble
real: hypothetical
says: collectors that float on the star's light instead of orbiting it

@mega dyson-shell
name: Dyson shell
real: hypothetical
says: one solid shell around the star; unstable without constant correction

@mega matrioshka-brain
name: Matrioshka brain
real: hypothetical
says: nested Dyson shells, each using the waste heat of the one inside, built to think instead of to live in

@mega stellar-engine
name: Stellar engine
real: hypothetical
says: a structure that moves a whole star, by pushing on its light from one side

@mega star-ring
name: Star ring
real: hypothetical
says: a vast spinning band around a star, its inner face a land to live on

@mega topopolis
name: Topopolis
real: hypothetical
says: an endless tube habitat wrapped around a star

@mega space-elevator
name: Space elevator
real: hypothetical
says: a cable from the ground to orbit, so cargo climbs to space instead of riding rockets

@mega orbital-ring
name: Orbital ring
real: hypothetical
says: a spinning ring around a planet, with cables hanging down to the ground

@mega planet-shield
name: Planet-wide shield
real: hypothetical
says: a giant magnetic or physical shield protecting a planet from its star or from weapons

# ── Space habitats and stations ──

@habitat station
name: Orbital station
real: yes
says: a crewed outpost in orbit, from a small lab to a city

@habitat stanford-torus
name: Stanford torus
real: hypothetical
says: a spinning wheel about 1.7 km wide, with gravity from the spin

@habitat bernal-sphere
name: Bernal sphere
real: hypothetical
says: a spinning hollow ball up to about 16 km wide

@habitat oneill-cylinder
name: O'Neill cylinder
real: hypothetical
says: twin spinning cylinders with whole landscapes on their inner walls, made to feel like home gravity

@habitat asteroid-habitat
name: Hollowed asteroid
real: hypothetical
says: a habitat dug inside an asteroid and spun for gravity

@habitat shipyard
name: Shipyard
real: yes
says: a station where ships are built

@habitat refinery
name: Orbital refinery
real: yes
says: a station that turns mined rock and ice into metal and fuel

# ── Ships by job ──

@ship probe
name: Probe
real: yes
says: an uncrewed explorer

@ship lander
name: Lander
real: yes
says: lands on a world's surface

@ship shuttle
name: Shuttle
real: yes
says: carries crew and cargo between the ground and orbit

@ship freighter
name: Freighter
real: yes
says: hauls cargo between worlds

@ship miner
name: Mining ship
real: yes
says: mines asteroids, comets and rings

@ship tanker
name: Fuel scoop tanker
real: yes
says: skims fuel from giant planets

@ship colony-ship
name: Colony ship
real: yes
says: carries settlers to found a new colony

@ship generation-ship
name: Generation ship
real: hypothetical
says: a ship so slow that its crew live and die aboard for generations before it arrives

@ship seed-ship
name: Seed ship
real: hypothetical
says: carries frozen life or genes instead of living crew

@ship warship
name: Warship
real: yes
says: built to fight

@ship carrier
name: Carrier
real: yes
says: carries smaller craft into battle

@ship world-grinder
name: World grinder
real: game
says: a huge moving machine, powered by atomics and a Dyson sphere, that eats whole worlds like a lawnmower crossing a lawn (Dark Harvest)

# ── Drives ──

@drive chemical
name: Chemical rocket
real: yes
says: burns fuel and oxidizer; proven but needs huge amounts of fuel

@drive ion
name: Ion drive
real: yes
says: electricity pushes charged gas out very fast; tiny thrust, huge efficiency, months to build speed

@drive solar-sail
name: Light sail
real: yes
says: a huge thin sail pushed by starlight; weaker the farther from the star

@drive magnetic-sail
name: Magnetic sail
real: hypothetical
says: rides the star's wind with a magnetic field

@drive nuclear-thermal
name: Nuclear-thermal rocket
real: yes
says: a reactor heats the propellant; about twice as efficient as the best chemical rockets

@drive nuclear-pulse
name: Nuclear-pulse drive
real: hypothetical
says: rides a chain of small atomic blasts against a pusher plate

@drive fusion
name: Fusion drive
real: hypothetical
says: fusion exhaust, hundreds of times more efficient than chemical rockets

@drive antimatter
name: Antimatter drive
real: hypothetical
says: matter meeting antimatter; the most energy per kilogram of any fuel

@drive laser-sail
name: Laser-pushed sail
real: hypothetical
says: a sail pushed by giant lasers from home, to a good fraction of light speed

@drive warp
name: Warp drive
real: hypothetical
says: bends space around the ship instead of moving through it; allowed on paper but needs exotic matter

@drive hyperdrive
name: Hyperdrive
real: game
says: jumps through hyperspace between stars; in Universe the step up from slower-than-light travel, growing into jump gates, wormhole networks and galaxy-to-galaxy jumps

@drive wormhole
name: Wormhole travel
real: hypothetical
says: a shortcut tunnel through space, held open with exotic matter

# ── Generator rules ──

@rule tech-seed
real: rule
says: every station, ship and megastructure is generated live; nothing is pre-built

@rule tech-own-image
real: rule
says: built things follow the builder species' genes and body plan: an insect species builds insect ships, stations and cities

@rule tech-ladder
real: rule
says: what a civilization can build follows its place on the 100-step travel ladder and its tech branches

@rule tech-kardashev
real: rule
says: Dyson swarms and spheres mark a stellar (Type II) civilization; galactic megastructures mark Type III

@rule tech-conditions
real: rule
says: colonies need the tech for every condition of their new world (the 10 × 10 world matrix)

@rule tech-resources
real: rule
says: every build costs resources from the 100 space resources; megastructures can strip whole planets

@rule tech-hypothetical
real: rule
says: real-but-unbuilt designs are allowed in the game; they unlock late and are marked hypothetical in content

# ── Dyson builds: the steps of enclosing a star, each made of parts (sizes in AU from the star) ──
# of: the megastructure it is a step of (its name from there); suffix: added to that name. star-bright: how much of the
# star's light still gets out (1 all). outer-au: how far out it reaches.
# part: one piece of it, any number of them:
#   mirrors COUNT FROM-AU TO-AU            mirror satellites orbiting, catching light
#   swarm COUNT RINGS BRIGHTNESS           collectors on tilted orbits round about 1 AU (dark panels that glint blue)
#   bubble COUNT                           light sails held still by the star's own light: a thin even sphere
#   shell RADIUS-AU LAND MODE [R G B GLOW] a solid shell (LAND yes: lived on inside; MODE 0 whole, 1 a ring band, 2 part
#                                          built, 3 a one-sided cap; R G B GLOW: its hull's colour and glow)
#   jet COUNT                              the light pushed out one way, as a long glowing plume (a stellar engine)
@build mirrors
name: Mirror satellites (the first step)
part: mirrors 500 0.5 0.9

@build dyson-swarm
of: dyson-swarm
part: swarm 30000 40 0.7
star-bright: 0.8

@build star-ring
of: star-ring
part: shell 1 yes 1

@build dyson-bubble
of: dyson-bubble
part: bubble 24000
star-bright: 0.7

@build part-shell
of: dyson-shell
suffix: , part-built
part: shell 1 yes 2

@build dyson-shell
of: dyson-shell
part: shell 1 yes 0
star-bright: 0

@build matrioshka-brain
of: matrioshka-brain
part: shell 0.4 no 0 0.5 0.12 0.08 0.6
part: shell 0.9 no 2 0.38 0.12 0.08 0.42
part: shell 1.8 no 2 0.26 0.12 0.08 0.24
star-bright: 0
outer-au: 1.8

@build stellar-engine
of: stellar-engine
part: shell 1 no 3 0.85 0.86 0.9 0.45
part: jet 3000

@build dimmed-swarm
of: dyson-swarm
suffix: , finished (the star is nearly hidden)
part: swarm 70000 160 0.5
star-bright: 0.2
